<id/17/1764/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Truffles"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <customs-1866/fungus/#concept> ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_fruits_nuts_vegetables/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "the *Tuber cibarium*, a fungus found in the earth beneath trees, especially oaks, beeches, and hawthorns. Being nutritious, fragrant, and stimulating in its properties, the truffle is a common ingredient in sauces and made dishes. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 402]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_fruits_nuts_vegetables): Named fruit, nut or vegetable left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 5 rows, 1800–1800. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×5. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×5. Top routes: France → United Kingdom ×1; Holland → United Kingdom ×1; World → United Kingdom ×1; Germany → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1764" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Truffles"@en ;
